From 392c8383c9ae9121c36ea498ccd787c095e274ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:33:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] repark accounting: blocked and parent-gated
 shared-clear wakes end the premise streak

Follow-up to PR #2932 (review https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/2932#pullrequestreview-5901683733,
nit 1; card t_01a1d85c5a382f3e). Not a regression: main behaved the same before #2932.

Why-chain
- Why 1: a card woken by a shared-blocker clear can still escalate on its next re-park.
- Why 2: `kanban_awaiting.prior_same_premise` ends the same-premise streak at a `shared_blocker_cleared`
  event only when its payload status is `ready`/`review`, so it can tell a real wake from a hold-retirement
  annotation (which carries no status).
- Why 3: two real wakes do not carry such a status. The blocked branch of `release_cleared_blockers`
  unblocks the card through `unblock_task` and appends the clear event with no status. `kwc._wake` lands
  `todo` (not `ready`) when parents are still open.
- Root cause: wake provenance was inferred from a status field that only one wake path wrote, and only
  for two of its three outcomes.

Fix
- `release_cleared_blockers` stamps `woke: true` on the clear event of every real wake (blocked branch
  and `_wake` branch). Annotation-only clears (ready/review cards, cards parked on their own wait) stay
  unchanged: no `woke`, no `status`.
- `prior_same_premise` ends the streak on `woke: true`, and also on the legacy `status` values `ready`,
  `review` and `todo` (events written before this change).

Tests (RED on base production modules 20c99f7a67, GREEN here)
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_blocker_park_wake.py: +4
  - test_blocked_clear_wake_ends_repark_streak (RED: 2 == 0)
  - test_parent_gated_clear_wake_ends_repark_streak (RED: 2 == 0)
  - test_clear_annotation_keeps_repark_streak[ready|own-wait] (controls: pass before and after)
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_awaiting.py: +3
  - test_clear_wake_provenance_resets_repark_budget[woke|woke+status None|status todo]
- The existing test_clear_annotation_does_not_reset_repark_budget[None|scheduled] stays green.
